R=Path(__file__).parent;d=pd.read_csv(R/'nfl-all-32-metrics.csv');s=d[d.scope.eq('season-to-date')];w=d[d.scope.eq('week-4')].set_index('team');cards=json.load(open(R/'selected-six-input.json'));a=json.load(open(R/'nfl-audit.json'));c=pd.read_csv(R/'college-selected-cohort-provisional.csv');cs=c[c.scope.eq('season-to-date')].sort_values('ap_rank')
prior=json.load(open(R.parent/'three-numbers-2026-09-29/college-audit.json'));prev={x['team'] for x in prior['selection']};cur=set(cs.team)
parts=['# THE DiRT CANON — THREE NUMBERS','Research cutoff: October 6, 2026, 8:44 a.m. America/New_York (EDT).','2026 NFL Week 4: October 1–5, including Monday night. Season-to-date cards: September 9–October 5. All 32 teams played; no Week 4 byes. NFL raw source refreshed October 6 at 8:13:37 a.m. EDT.','CFB completed Week 5: October 1–3 local game dates (late Saturday games can finish October 4 Eastern). Latest selection: October 4 AP Top 10, feed timestamp October 4 at 5:10 p.m. EDT. College source refreshed October 5 at 11:38:34 a.m. EDT. College calculations remain provisional; see hold below.','## Six public cards — season to date','Values below are computed from frozen play-level inputs. Higher net is better. NFL ranks compare all 32 teams.']
for row in cards:
 t=row['team_code'];v=s[s.team.eq(t)].iloc[0];vweek=w.loc[t]
 parts+=['### '+row['team'],row['verdict'].replace('\n',' '),f"Efficiency: {v.net_epa:+.3f} net EPA/play (NFL #{v.epa_rank}); consistency: {v.net_success:+.1f} percentage points (#{v.success_rank}); big-play balance: {v.net_explosive:+.1f} percentage points (#{v.explosive_rank}).",f"Week 4 only: {vweek.net_epa:+.3f} net EPA/play; {vweek.net_success:+.1f} success percentage points; {vweek.net_explosive:+.1f} explosive percentage points. The public card describes all four games, not just this week.",f"Sample: {v.off_plays} offensive and {v.def_plays} defensive eligible plays. Next: {v.next_opponent}. Four games remain a small, unadjusted sample; opponent quality and personnel can change the interpretation."]
parts+=['## Every NFL team','| Team | Net EPA/play (rank) | Success balance, percentage points (rank) | Explosive balance, percentage points (rank) | Off / def plays |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for _,v in s.sort_values('epa_rank').iterrows():parts.append(f"| {v['name']} | {v.net_epa:+.3f} ({v.epa_rank}) | {v.net_success:+.1f} ({v.success_rank}) | {v.net_explosive:+.1f} ({v.explosive_rank}) | {v.off_plays} / {v.def_plays} |")
parts+=['## All-team written points']
for _,v in s.iterrows():
 parts += ['### '+v['name'],f"{v['name']} ranks {v.epa_rank} in efficiency, {v.success_rank} in consistency and {v.explosive_rank} in big-play balance. Its four-game net efficiency is {v.net_epa:+.3f} EPA per play. These are unadjusted results, not settled talent. Next checkpoint: {v.next_opponent}; watch whether the weakest rank improves without giving back the strongest."]
parts+=['## College — provisional research table, not public cards','AP position is selection, not our metric ranking. The following metric ranks compare only these ten selected teams, NOT all FBS teams. No newcomers or departures from the prior selected cohort.' if cur==prev else f'Newcomers: {cur-prev}; departures: {prev-cur}.','| AP | Team | Games | Net EPA/play | Success balance, percentage points | Explosive balance, percentage points | Cohort ranks: E / C / B |','|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for _,v in cs.iterrows():parts.append(f"| {v.ap_rank} | {v.team} | {v.games} | {v.net_epa:+.3f} | {v.net_success:+.1f} | {v.net_explosive:+.1f} | {int(v.epa_selected_cohort_rank)} / {int(v.success_selected_cohort_rank)} / {int(v.explosive_selected_cohort_rank)} |")
parts+=['Texas and Ole Miss had no Week 5 game in the selection. Their weekly metrics are missing, never zero performance. LSU is already AP No. 10, so no eleventh team is added.','COLLEGE HOLD: the independent weekly schedule feeds returned only 25 events each, while the dataset contains 390 FBS-involving games and 59 in Week 5. All 250 team scores in the retrieved 125-game schedule subset match, but that is not a complete FBS audit. One exact duplicate row was removed; no conflicting duplicate game/row IDs remain. There are 95 eligible plays without EPA. Source classification/penalty handling still needs a complete reconciliation before public CFB cards or national ranks.','The production renderer currently hardcodes NFL rank labels. It was not modified to mislabel college cards. College tables and raw calculations are provided for review only.','## Methodology','Version: three-numbers-eligible-v1, continuing the prior issue. Efficiency = mean offensive EPA minus mean defensive EPA allowed. Expected points added estimates how a play changes the offense’s expected scoring value given the game situation. Consistency = share of eligible modeled plays with EPA > 0 on offense minus the corresponding defensive share. Big-play balance = share of all eligible snaps with a completed pass gain of at least 20 yards or a rush gain of at least 10 yards, generated minus allowed. Success/explosive differences use percentage points: 50% minus 40% equals 10 percentage points, not 10%.','NFL eligibility follows nflfastR run/pass classification, including sacks and scrambles, excluding kneels, spikes, no-plays, conversions and special teams. Penalty plays retain the source run/pass result only when a valid scrimmage play remains; no_play rows are excluded. Overtime is included. No garbage-time filter or opponent adjustment is applied. Missing EPA is excluded from both EPA and success denominators, never zero-filled. NFL coverage this run: 7,789 eligible plays, zero missing EPA or yards.','College uses the single cfbfastR EPA source, with rush/pass_attempt/sack flags, penalty_no_play exclusion and the documented text/type exclusions in compute_college.py. These provisional classifications are unchanged from the prior issue and are not represented as fully audited. NFL and college raw EPA scales are not treated as interchangeable.','Season results pool plays; they are not averages of game averages. Ranks use minimum rank for ties. Percentiles = 100 × (N − rank)/(N − 1), a rank-based descriptive convention, not probability. All NFL teams have four games, so a last-four-team-games window equals the season-to-date window here. Prior NFL published rank changes are included in CSV; no prior college national ranks are invented.','Selection: all 32 NFL teams were calculated first. Editorial shortlist: SF/BAL dominance, ATL/ARI/GB contradictions and MIA weakness. The repository selector orders those six; its interest ordering is editorial, not a predictive power rating.','## Coverage and visual audit','NFL: 64 of 64 season final scores match the independent ESPN feed. Week 4: 16 of 16 finals, all 32 teams’ offensive play and total-yard counts match the box-score feed. No duplicate NFL game/play IDs. No missing Week 4 game or postponement appears in the retrieved NFL slate. College coverage is provisional as above.','Current main-branch renderer code retrieved October 6. The retrieved compass blob (Git SHA 31a3508cb8472fb92b24f39d408551f870be8fc0) is a broken PNG. This run restores the user-supplied original, SHA256 9f6fbe5cb5437abf7a22c79d59083ac7d36ba864befe33571954cc3b5838fbdd. Layout code is unchanged. This local asset restoration is NOT a claim that the remote repository has been repaired.','Six 1080×1350 cards were rendered with the required command. Text fit is enforced by the renderer. No image model was used. Missing team emblems are left empty per the repository asset instructions. Public metrics, units, rank labels, centered compass, THREE NUMBERS title and site footer were inspected; OCR results and per-card layout records are included.','## Sources and attribution','- nflverse/nflfastR data: https://github.com/nflverse/nflverse-data/releases/download/pbp/play_by_play_2026.csv.gz (CC BY 4.0; derived calculations by The DiRT Canon).','- NFL variable documentation: https://nflfastr.com/articles/field_descriptions.html','- College documented source: https://cfbfastr.sportsdataverse.org/reference/load_cfb_pbp.html','- College release: https://github.com/sportsdataverse/sportsdataverse-data/releases/tag/cfbfastR_cfb_pbp','- AP selection feed: https://site.api.espn.com/apis/site/v2/sports/football/college-football/rankings?season=2026&seasontype=2&week=6','- Schedule and box-score feed URLs and retrieval timestamps are recorded in source/retrieval.json and source/checks-retrieval.json.','- Source version/model IDs are not embedded in every feed. File hashes fix the exact input snapshot; no claim of unchanged underlying model training is made.','- College data reuse terms were not independently resolved for redistribution: the large raw college parquet is not bundled. The package records its URL/hash and provides derived provisional values.','- Rendering: https://github.com/xrupert/dirt-canon-collective/tree/main/content_os','- No email attachment, external publication or additional automation was created.']
(R/'report.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(parts))
